# OpenCrossing (Animal Crossing) — gt-input-remap shim gptk.
# For this port the shim drives keyboard STATE synthesis directly from the
# gamepad's evdev device (launcher sets GT_EVDEV_KEYS=1) because AC's stock
# 32-bit SDL 2.0.12 delivers no joystick/controller events to the game at all.
#
# AC's keybindings.ini binds (SDL scancode names):
#   A=Space  B=Left Shift  X=X  Y=Y  L=Q  R=E  Z=Z  Start=Return
#   Main Stick=W/A/S/D   C-Stick(camera)=arrows
# The RG SP has no analog stick, so the D-pad drives the Main Stick (walking);
# L2/R2 rotate the camera (C-stick left/right).
#
# Face buttons map STRAIGHT to AC's keybindings.ini: gptk `a`->game A (Space),
# `b`->game B (Left Shift), `x`->game X, `y`->game Y. F48 (device gate,
# 2026-09-01): the shim now applies the Nintendo/Xbox layout swap dynamically
# from GT_CONTROLLER_LAYOUT, so this file is the un-swapped Nintendo baseline.
# The earlier F45 static cross-assignment (a<->b, x<->y) double-applied with the
# new shim swap and came out exactly reversed on device, so it was removed.
# Device-confirmed 2026-09-01: A/B/X/Y correct in both layouts.
up = w
down = s
left = a
right = d
a = space
b = left_shift
x = x
y = y
l1 = q
r1 = e
l2 = left
r2 = right
back = z
start = enter
